

NTPINFO(1)          UNIX Programmer's Manual             NTPINFO(1)



NAME
     ntpinfo - print the structure of a NinjaTracker+ module

SYNOPSIS
     ntpinfo file

DESCRIPTION
     _N_t_p_i_n_f_o reads a NinjaTracker+ (.ntp) module and prints its
     header, name, oscillator assignments, and instrument table in
     hexadecimal.  It is an inspector for the modules that ntp-
     play(1) performs; it does not open the sound hardware.

     The screen is cleared, then the following are printed:

     NTP vVV trk TT ins II pat PP ord OO
            The format version and the counts of tracks, instru-
            ments, patterns, and order-list entries.

     name NAME
            The module's embedded name.

     osc XX XX ...
            One byte per track: the oscillator that voice plays
            on.

     iNN tTT LLLL vVV
            One entry per instrument, two per line: index, type,
            sample length, and volume.  The instrument's own name
            is read past but not shown.

     All numeric fields are hexadecimal.

DIAGNOSTICS
     _N_t_p_i_n_f_o prints and exits nonzero on: a missing file argument
     (usage), a file it cannot open (cannot open), a header whose
     magic is not "nfc!" (bad magic), or a file that ends before
     the structure is fully read (short read).

SEE ALSO
     ntpplay(1)

